 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only one challenging case is confirmed: scene 19f339ba with the car 1 s early, at 0.5x speed, and the ego at 1.2x its recorded speed (S22). Every repeat there failed, and its 90% range lies above 0.5. All confirmed failures and most of the hints come from this one highway scene. There, after hand-off, the policy braked hard with no lead car close ahead and drifted left. It then hit the car in the left lane, or was side-swiped by a replayed car coming up from behind. In that scene the ego's hand-off speed seems to matter more than the retimed car's timing or speed: failures appeared across many car settings at 1.0x ego speed and above, and none at 0.6x or 0.8x. That pattern rests on one run per setting, so it is a hint, not a rate. No other scene produced a failure the policy was confirmed to cause, and none of the failures carry possible simulator artifacts.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "The one confirmed challenging case is scene 19f339ba with the car 1 s early, at 0.5x speed, and the ego at 1.2x. Every repeat failed, and the 90% range lies above 0.5. In each run the policy braked hard on an open highway with no lead nearby, drifted left, and either hit actor 1 in the left lane or was struck on the side by the replayed actor 28.",
